_:hammer_and_wrench: Refactor suggestion_

**Check for scaling issues with the admin ID comparison.**  
The for-loop sets `userType` to `'Admin'` if the member’s `_id` matches the one admin in `admins[0]`. If multiple admins exist, only one would ever be recognized here. Consider iterating over all admins and marking each admin properly.  

```diff
-for (let i = 0; i < allMembers.length; i++) {
-  if (allMembers[i]._id === adminId) {
-    allMembers[i].userType = 'Admin';
-  } else {
-    allMembers[i].userType = 'Member';
-  }
-}
+if (admins && admins.length > 0) {
+  const adminIds = admins.map((adm) => adm._id);
+  for (let i = 0; i < allMembers.length; i++) {
+    if (adminIds.includes(allMembers[i]._id)) {
+      allMembers[i].userType = 'Admin';
+    } else {
+      allMembers[i].userType = 'Member';
+    }
+  }
+}
```


